; perf_ai_4b (plan row P304, ADR 0038 section 7): the AI arena of Phase 4b. It plays perf_ai's layout (the base arena's
; map and factions, the mirror bases) with each side's Phase 4b rows at tick 0, so the ARMY slot's new passes run from the
; first think: a Flight Yard, 2 Burst Stacks (Sky Needles for the Lumen Accord), an Engineering Centre, a Space Centre
; (charged at tick 0, its 2700 ticks, as perf_ai charges its strike building, so a sweep can fire inside the run), two more
; Power Plants for them, 2 bombers, 2 fighters, 2 transports and 4 drone squads. The ten mobile rows come off the light
; tanks (4) and the rifle squads (6), which keeps each side at the rules' 75-unit cap. All on frozen copies of the Phase 4b
; defs in data/dev/arena/ (2026-11-15, main a2204d2f): the Derrick League's aircraft, Flight Yard, Burst Stack and rifle and
; rocket squads are perf_air's own (air/ and units/), the rest P304's.
; P304b (2026-11-17, main e4be1931) adds each side's ground carriers and minelayers, 2 of each (the Bunk Wagon and Shot Truck, the
; Linecar and Seeder: frozen copies in arena_4b/units/ and arena_4b/weapons/), 4 mobile rows a side taken off the rifle squads
; (18 to 14), so each side stays at the 75-unit cap. The AI does not load, unload or mine with them yet.
; Own copies in data/dev/arena/arena_4b/: the rules (the base arena's frozen rules plus today's sell, mend, carry, mine and
; sweep values, flow_cache_size 8 as perf_ai, so carriers and mending work here), and the infantry and turret units with
; their shipped layer masks (the Lumen rifle and rocket squads and the Derrick turret shoot at aircraft as shipped, as
; perf_air's squads do). No orders, no golden pair: the hash is printed, not pinned. The Perf AI route plays it with the
; frozen AI defs of data/dev/arena/ai_4b/.

